Not allowed
- Giving an AI the assignment and asking it to do the assignment, in whole or in large part.
- Having an AI write the core networking code. You write these yourself; an AI may review them after you have written them:
- framing - encoding a message, and reading one from the stream. In the Python starter these are encode and read_message; in the C starter, etp_send and etp_read_header;
- the transport seam: the six functions in your transport_tcp file;
- the server's session handling and concurrency: the request loop, the checks of Specification §8.1, and how sessions run side by side;
- the client's session: HELLO, the command, BYE, and the choice of exit status.
- Having an AI produce your answers to Q1-Q5 or your etp-facts values, or read your capture and tell you the values to write down - including having it write a command or
script that pulls those values out for you. An AI may teach you how tshark or a display filter works; the reading of your own capture is yours. The values come from your own capture and the reasoning is in your own words.
